  "change": "Verify that an unavailable active vault root produces a safe refresh error while retaining the existing listing, fails closed on preview, and recovers to exact updated bytes after the same root returns without vault or app-data writes.",
  "focused_test": {
    "name": "egui_failed_vault_refresh_retains_listing_and_recovers_after_root_returns_without_writing",
    "command": "cargo test --workspace --locked",
    "result": "Passed on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows GitHub Actions jobs.",
    "log_lines": {
      "ubuntu": "test tests::egui_failed_vault_refresh_retains_listing_and_recovers_after_root_returns_without_writing ... ok",
      "macos": "test tests::egui_failed_vault_refresh_retains_listing_and_recovers_after_root_returns_without_writing ... ok",
      "windows": "test tests::egui_failed_vault_refresh_retains_listing_and_recovers_after_root_returns_without_writing ... ok"
    }
  },
  "scenario_result": [
    "Opened a one-note vault with a valid BOM/CRLF preview and a separate app-data sentinel, then moved the selected vault directory away from its canonical root. Refresh reported the safe error while retaining the original session, one-note listing, and selected relative path.",
    "Requesting the selected note preview while the root was unavailable failed closed with no source preview and an explicit error. Vault contents at the relocated path and separate app data remained unchanged.",
    "Externally updated the note under the relocated root, restored that same directory to its original path, refreshed successfully, and verified the prior errors cleared while the selected path remained active. The fresh preview matched the exact updated bytes.",
    "Full vault and separate app-data snapshots remained unchanged through failed refresh, failed preview, root restoration, successful refresh and preview, and UI teardown."
  ],
